{"id": "EUVD-2026-108830", "enisaUuid": "c6f7392f-713d-3dbf-b03d-6697737f3eea", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmmc: mtk-sd: Cancel request timeout work on remove\n\nThe driver queues req_timeout while a request is active.\nmsdc_request_done() uses cancel_delayed_work(), which does not wait for\na timeout callback that has already started.\n\nThe timeout callback calls mmc_request_done(), which wakes the request\nwaiter, and then continues to use host->dev_comp and check the SDIO IRQ.\nDuring unbind, msdc_drv_remove() can return and the managed mmc_host can\nbe freed before the callback finishes.\n\nKASAN reported use-after-free accesses in msdc_request_done() and\nmsdc_recheck_sdio_irq() in each of three unbind tests.  The same tests\ncompleted without a kernel diagnostic after this change.\n\nCall cancel_delayed_work_sync() after mmc_remove_host() has stopped new\nrequests and before the driver releases the host resources.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:21:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:21:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e799f25c420e759641eb25102967ea091fc758f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f37e0367ad6f2147a0b37564b442b7a25bec0d23", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46e75703ca3f00fb8c935b3ce35b90836e34e8af", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/edef1355224c0799a502a46b71d3649fa0dd218e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b38af5386a74416e898955443f2e26547b358cb2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99035"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "038494a5-d54b-3811-8cea-fc68ae03200b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "0d4dc0bd-70ce-3a72-86e2-f861b25bb99e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "208489032bdd8d4a7de50f3057c175058f271956 <46e75703ca3f00fb8c935b3ce35b90836e34e8af"}, {"id": "29de4535-b66a-390c-bb37-9c4855f59a07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "208489032bdd8d4a7de50f3057c175058f271956 <f37e0367ad6f2147a0b37564b442b7a25bec0d23"}, {"id": "3dde43ec-d5f7-3b9b-9ee3-af6bc66b637c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "208489032bdd8d4a7de50f3057c175058f271956 <b38af5386a74416e898955443f2e26547b358cb2"}, {"id": "4533b85a-bb18-3f82-861c-55fcdba419d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "63be2095-3148-3841-953b-a40bcfc3eadd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "208489032bdd8d4a7de50f3057c175058f271956 <9e799f25c420e759641eb25102967ea091fc758f"}, {"id": "65ee65c9-4043-34e5-8c33-d3bd1906ba3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.2"}, {"id": "6cc8e4d2-b7ae-3c28-b4df-13ab57a26198", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8e62abc8-28f9-3f58-9b24-d00037ccc57d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "a55d5f48-e02d-3c90-ad05-26a5be6e43c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "adb71184-6f82-3d7a-b739-2352c216e8cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "208489032bdd8d4a7de50f3057c175058f271956 <edef1355224c0799a502a46b71d3649fa0dd218e"}, {"id": "ae4556f6-aa5d-31f0-a847-0ba8ebcdc570", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7aef2275-e913-37f1-9864-ed089fd9af13", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}